/*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  MEASURED-AND-CORRELATED vapour-liquid equilibrium of propene (1) + propane (2),
  SEVEN ISOTHERMS, 100-160 degF, nine liquid compositions each (63 rows) -- the
  fit case's evidence file.

  SOURCE (the page, not an archive): Laurance, D.R.; Swift, G.W.  "Relative
  Volatility of Propane-Propene System from 100-160 F", J. Chem. Eng. Data 17
  (1972) 333-336, Table IV "Results of Calculations" (p. 335).  The same rows as
  tutorials/props/compare/olefins01_propane_propene_laurance1972/constant/
  experiments (seven files there, one per isotherm), here in ONE file with the
  isotherm as a column, T in K, because a P_bubble fit reads the held
  temperature from each point and because the engine's guard refuses one
  sha256 as both fit and validation: THE SPLIT IS BY ROW (`discard` in
  system/propsDict).  Rows 1-9 are 100 F, 10-18 110 F, 19-27 120 F, 28-36 130 F,
  37-45 140 F, 46-54 150 F, 55-63 160 F.  FIT = 100, 120, 140, 160 F; HELD OUT =
  110, 130, 150 F (rows 10-18, 28-36, 46-54).  The check_olefin_vle gate holds
  these rows equal to olefins01's.

  What the numbers ARE: the vapour pressures of Table I were MEASURED (probable
  error 0.1 %) and correlated; Table IV COMPUTES y, P and alpha from them by
  integrating the isothermal coexistence equation (estimated error +-0.005 in
  alpha).  No vapour was sampled.  So the fit's residual is on P (the quantity
  the paper measured), and alpha is only what the gate recomputes afterwards.
  Two printed slips are declared in olefins01's headers (a P at 120 F, a y at
  110 F); the rows are as printed.  Pressure in psia.
\*--------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

property     binaryVLE.P_bubble;


provenance
{
    source       measured;
    reviewStatus transcribedNotCheckedAgainstArticle;
    citation     "Laurance, D.R.; Swift, G.W. (1972). Relative volatility of propane-propene system from 100-160 F. J. Chem. Eng. Data 17, 333-336, Table IV (p. 335). doi:10.1021/je60054a011";
    sourceFile   "laurance1972-propane-propene-relative-volatility.pdf";
    sha256       "604276ffa5904a88de50eb252f48c98117ec25fe4d7cbfff0e853299d222056b";   // of that PDF
}

columns
(
    { name x[propylene];  unit -;  }
    { name T;  unit K;  }
    { name P_bubble;  unit psi;  }
    { name y_eqT_propylene;  unit -;  }
    { name alpha;  unit -;  }
);

data
